X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Highland Brewing": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/truphonic/", "Where Y'at AVL Music": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/truphonic/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Highlandbrewing": "https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/truphonic/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:highlandbrewing
X-SOURCE:Highland Brewing, Where Y'at AVL Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T210000
DTSTAMP:20260913T194539Z
CREATED:20260912T200622Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260913T194539Z
UID:10029840-1791054000-1791061200@highlandbrewing.com
SUMMARY:Truphonic
DESCRIPTION:Bio\n\n\n\nThe original music of Jake Salter & a unique group of talented musicians come together in Tru Phonic. Sounds of Jam\, Funk\, Blues\, Rock\, Soul\, Jazz and Hip-Hop & more can be heard when seeing the band Live or on their Studio Albums. Established in 2017\, Tru Phonic includes Multiple veterans in the Central Florida music scene who have worked with many other great bands and musicians in the area. The group has an ever-changing\, high-energy live show that makes you wanna MOVE! Tru Phonic’s original sound is characterized by high skill-level shown on each instrument\, talented vocal harmonies\, powerful lyrics\, expanding grooves\, unique guitar playing & a tight horn section.   \n​In just a few years of touring Tru Phonic has made quite an impression everywhere they go\, establishing fanbases & regular listeners in cities allover the Southeast U.S. & Booking Music Festivals Like Suwannee Hulaween 2023\, Farm to Grass\, Whippersnap Music & arts Fest\, Sunshine Hootenany\, Everglades Roots Fest\, No Resolutions\, Fort20 Fest & more…. \nThe band also has a strong online presence & following with their original music accumulating steady numbers in just over 6 years; \n-over 230\,000 streams across all platforms \n-77\,000+ video views on FB & YouTube  \n-15\,000 + social followers  \n\n\n\nWeekend Live Music\nHighland Brewing’s weekend live music series showcases incredible local talent\, regional acts and national touring bands from across the East Coast and beyond. Free and open to all ages (unless noted otherwise)\, it’s the perfect excuse to gather your crew\, listen and vibe to a wide range of genres including soul\, bluegrass\, acoustic\, country\, folk and more.\nLive music typically takes place on our scenic Meadow stage. Shows are rain or shine\, if the weather doesn’t cooperate and we have time to move inside\, the band will play in the Taproom where there’s still plenty of room to boogie.\nChairs\, blankets and well-behaved\, leashed pets are welcome in the Meadow. Please note that coolers and outside alcohol are not permitted on the premises.
URL:https://highlandbrewing.com/calendar/truphonic/
LOCATION:Meadow at Highland Brewing Co.\, 12 Old Charlotte Highway\, Suite 200\, Asheville\, NC\, 28803\, United States
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://highlandbrewing.com/wp-content/uploads/Truphonic-Resize.png
END:VEVENT
