BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:trumba_calendars_buncombe_county_government_ics
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Government
SUMMARY:Buncombe County Parks Update - Open and Closed Parks
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Event Type";ID=21;TYPE=number:Park &amp\; Rec
 reation
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Email";ID=35519;TYPE=Email:<a href="mailto:pa
 rks@buncombecounty.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">parks@buncombecou
 nty.org</a>
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Phone";ID=35516;TYPE=PhoneUS10NoExt:(828) 250
 -4260
X-TRUMBA-CUSTOMFIELD;NAME="Notice - Description";ID=51963;TYPE=SingleLin
 e:Information about Open and Closed Parks
DTSTAMP:20250617T085331Z
DESCRIPTION:Email: parks@buncombecounty.org<br>Phone: (828) 250-4260<br>
 Notice - Description: Information about Open and Closed Parks<br><br>Man
 y Buncombe County Parks were impacted by Hurricane Helene.&#160\; While 
 we are working diligently reopen parks as quickly as we can\, some parks
  continue to remain closed. Please see the list below for which parks ar
 e open and which parks continue to be closed for safety reasons.<br><br>
 OPEN Parks:&#160\; Lake Julian Park (please note\, some disc golf holes 
 remain closed)\, Hominy Valley Park\, Collier Cove Nature Preserve\, Nor
 th Buncombe Fields\, Cane Creek Playground\, Buncombe County Sports Park
 \, Corcoran Paige River Park\, Bent Creek River Park\, Ledges Whitewater
  Park\, and Hominy Creek River Park.&#160\; If people choose to recreate
  on the river\, we strongly encourage them to be aware of changes on str
 eambanks and in the riverbed and the potential for unknown debris from H
 elene.<br><br>CLOSED Parks:&#160\; Charles D. Owen Park\, Karpen Soccer 
 Field\, Alexander River Park\, Walnut Island River Park\, and Glen Bridg
 e River Park*. *Note\, if the gate is open at Glen Bridge River Park\, i
 t may be used.&#160\; For safety reasons\, we ask the public not to ente
 r closed parks.<br><br>Please email <a href="mailto:parks@buncombecounty
 .org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">parks@buncombecounty.org</a> or cal
 l (828) 250-4260 with any questions or for additional information.
CATEGORIES:Parks &amp; Recreation
UID:http://uid.trumba.com/event/179136506
X-TRUMBA-LINK:https://www.buncombecounty.org/countycenter/events-calenda
 r.aspx?trumbaEmbed=view%3Devent%26eventid%3D179136506
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Amcdance": "https://www.meetup.com/amcdance/events/316669287/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_amcdance
X-SOURCE:Asheville Movement Collective
UID:event_316669287@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050017Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T123000
SUMMARY:Ecstatic Dance Waves w/ Robert Kochka & Amanda Crowe
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Movement Collective\nSunday\, October 4th\n1st Dance
  Wave 8:30\\-10:30am \\| Warmup 8:30am \\| Opening Circle 9am\n2nd Dance W
 ave 10:30\\-12:30am \\| Warmup 10:30am \\| Opening Circle 11am\nFacilitato
 r Robert Kochka and Amanda Crowe\n\nIntention: Loop of Infinity\n\nHow man
 y parts have been buried\, composted\,\nAlchemized\, reclaimed?\nHow many 
 different\nMaidens\, mothers\, crones\nHave I been?\nA lifetime spirals ou
 t\nFrom every exhale\nA new beginning\nWith every inhale\nEach version of 
 myself\nA full circle\,\nCreating my fractal identity\nGobsmacked and\nDru
 nk on eternity\nAt the pinpoint of timelines\nCollapsing and expanding\nLi
 ke a star birthing a galaxy\nAn infinite loop of\nPast\, future\, and pres
 ent\nWrapped in\nEvery\nSingle\nMoment\nTime melting on my tongue\nIs an a
 lchemic elixir\nEvery second is a chance\nFor Transmutation\nPoem by Alia 
 Alsaif Spiers\nPainting: Amanda Crowe\n\n## About Robert Kochka and Amanda
  Crowe\n\nRobert Kochka’s amazing dance waves and DJ sets are known for 
 their fullness: bass\, feeling\, and energy! You’ll dance\, you’ll mov
 e\, you’ll feel new vibrations! Listen to his sets here: [https://soundc
 loud.com/robert-kochka-jr](https://soundcloud.com/robert-kochka-jr)\n\nAma
 nda Crowe sets and holds a wonderful container seeded with intention and b
 eauty.\n\nThis pair will lay out the carpet to welcome you more deeply int
 o yourself\, and perhaps into togetherness on the dance floor.\n\\~\\~\\~\
 n\n\\*\\* Please note that the dance starts at Warm up. The doors close pr
 omptly at Opening Circle and any that come late will be turned away. Pleas
 e be on time to ensure a safe and secure container. \\*\\*\nTicket Prices:
  $15 - $30 or name your price.\n\nNo one turned away for lack of funds!\nP
 re-registration Recommended:\n\nVOLUNTEER!\n\nWe need volunteers. Voluntee
 r and dance for free! Register to volunteer at:\n[https://ashevillemovemen
 tcollective.org/volunteer/](https://ashevillemovementcollective.org/volunt
