X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Runners": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/315933573/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_runners
X-SOURCE:Asheville Runners
UID:event_315933573@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050018Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T200000
SUMMARY:Thursday Run 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Runners\nCome run 1\, 3\, or 6 miles and stay for a 
 beer and soccer tennis after at Olde London Road.\n\nRoutes-\n1 miler:\nRI
 GHT out of OLR parking lot\nContinue around roundabout at Clingman\, and h
 ead toward the river on Lyman St.\nRIGHT on River Arts Place\nCross Rivers
 ide onto the Greenway\nRight on the Greenway to the Craven St Park put in 
 (the dock)\nTurn around and go back the same way to OLR\n\n3 miler:\nStart
  the same as 1 miler\nContinue onto Craven St. Bridge\nLEFT onto Greenway 
 after bridge\nFollow Greenway all the way until it ends at Haywood Rd.\nRI
 GHT onto Haywood Rd\, go across the bridge\nCross the Roundabout at Robert
 s St. and continue onto Clingman\nContinue on Clingman\nLEFT onto Owens Be
 ll Lane\nLEFT onto Hilliard at the top of the hill\nLEFT onto W Haywood\, 
 follow all the way down to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts\nFollow Roberts back
  to OLR\nPass OLR to Bartlett\, turn around and come back to OLR\n\n6 mile
 r:\nAfter the W Haywood downhill to Roberts\nLEFT onto Roberts St. take to
  Lyman and head back to the Greenway\nLEFT onto the Greenway\, take all th
 e way to Amboy\nRIGHT on Amboy to cross the bridge\nRIGHT into French Broa
 d River Park\, run the loop at the park\nCross back over the bridge on Amb
 oy and run the Greenway back to the roundabout\nFollow Lyman back to OLR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-runners/events/315933573/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260801T141836Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260801T141836Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/the-botanical-series-the-reserve/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T200000
DTSTAMP:20260922T180916Z
CREATED:20260922T163724Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T180916Z
UID:1778780019795-1791482400-1791489600@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:The Botanical Series: The Reserve
DESCRIPTION:The Botanical Series: The Reserve\nThursday\, October 8\, 2026 from 6 to 8 p.m.\nBlue Ridge Court at The North Carolina Arboretum\n\n\n\n\nAn elevated evening. A distinct Arboretum experience.\n  \nThe North Carolina Arboretum and Chemist Spirits have come together to create a one-of-a-kind botanical vodka inspired by the plants and landscapes of Western North Carolina. Developed through months of collaboration\, the spirit features botanicals thoughtfully harvested from the Arboretum and transformed by Chemist Spirits into a distinctive expression of place. \nThe Reserve offers an intimate opportunity to experience that collaboration at its most refined. Set against the mountain backdrop of Blue Ridge Court\, this limited-capacity evening pairs botanical spirits\, food and live music with a curated tasting experience led by Chemist Spirits. \nExplore the flavors and botanicals behind the spirit before creating your own botanical-infused cocktail\, guided by the experts who developed it. Then settle in and enjoy the evening with live music and heavy hors d’oeuvres in one of the Arboretum’s most beautiful settings. \nEach guest will also receive a commemorative 40th Anniversary Arboretum tasting glass to take home. Parking is included. \nPlease note: This event is for guests ages 21 and older. A valid photo ID will be required for age verification upon arrival. \nLearn more and purchase tickets here.
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/the-botanical-series-the-reserve/
