X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/315644648/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_315644648@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050031Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
SUMMARY:Let's Walk: It's Leaf Season at the NC Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nMeet inside the Baker Vis
 itor Center. Restrooms are available at the start point. We will start wal
 king as soon as everyone has arrived.\n\nThe walk is a guided 5 KM trail. 
 There are some moderate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of th
 e route is on well-groomed trails with very few obstacles. Some people wil
 l want walking poles.\n\nWe will walk down Wesley Branch Trail to Bent Cre
 ek Road. Traveling down Bent Creek Road\, we will loop through the Azalea 
 Garden a little further than we usually go. The Azaleas won't be in bloom\
 , but it will be leaf season after all. We will continue down Bent Creek R
 oad\, returning to the parking lot via Wolf Branch Road and Greenhouse Way
 . Before we quit\, we will walk through the Bonsai Exhibition Garden and t
 he Formal Gardens.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen
 . Sneakers should be fine\, unless it has rained recently. Be sure to brin
 g **plenty of water** and a protein snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome bu
 t are not allowed in buildings or in the Bonsai Exhibit. Trail strollers s
 hould be ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an admission fee\, but they
  charge $25 per car parking fee (so pack as many people in your car as you
  can). We recommend the driver purchase the lowest level annual membership
  which includes free parking. (Of course\, you may want a higher-level mem
 bership\, your choice.) We walk at the Arboretum at least six times per ye
 ar.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315644648/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260711T193020Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260711T193020Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/sound-bath-october-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T113000
DTSTAMP:20260904T194335Z
CREATED:20260904T194335Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T194335Z
UID:1778780019782-1792231200-1792236600@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Sound Bath in the Gardens
DESCRIPTION:Sound Bath\nwith Asheville Wellness Tours \nSaturday\, October 17  |  10 – 11:30 am \nRegister Here!\nExperience the magic of Sound Baths in the Gardens. While relaxing amongst the flora\, be soothed by the sounds of unique instruments used to reset your nervous system. This 60-minute pause from your day-to-day will be nestled in the gardens of The NC Arboretum: a nature home away from home. If it’s raining\, don’t worry. There is a beautiful indoor space with large windows overlooking the forest so you can still soak in the magic without being actually soaked. \nYour ticket grants you access into The NC Arboretum (feel free to explore their exhibits afterwards!). You can bring your own mat or borrow one of ours for $5. \n Asheville Wellness Tours offers customizable wellness and yoga retreats and experiences in the mountains of Western North Carolina. While our mission is to help you reconnect with yourself\, with others\, and with nature\, we’re also here to have fun! We love to intertwine interesting\, insightful\, and rejuvenating experiences so you can enjoy a truly meaningful time here in beautiful Asheville. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/sound-bath-october-2026/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/album-cover.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-10-17/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
DTSTAMP:20260710T074430Z
CREATED:20260710T074430Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260710T074430Z
UID:1778780019631-1792231200-1792238400@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Guided Trail Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hit the trails and learn more about The North Carolina Arboretum’s botanically diverse forest with a guided trail walk! April through October\, this free hiking program is led by trained volunteer guides who take small groups of participants along woodland trails and through a variety of forest types. Depending on the season and each guide’s area of expertise\, topics of discussion may include wildflowers\, plant and tree identification\, natural history and more. \nGuided trail walks are limited to 15 people\, including the guide\, and are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age. Groups depart from the Baker Visitor Center Lobby on Tuesdays at 1 p.m. and Saturdays at 10 a.m. and 1 p.m.. \nWalks last 1.5 – 2.5 hours\, are approximately one to two miles in length. As this program is held rain or shine\, all participants should dress appropriately for the weather. \nThere is no pre-registration; walks are first-come first served and sign up sheets are located in the Baker Visitors Center. \nWalks are FREE; however\, donations to The North Carolina Arboretum Society are appreciated. Regular parking fees apply. Arboretum Society Members always park free. \nKnow Before You Go\n\nGuided Trail Walks are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age.\nGuided Trail Walks are rain or shine and all participants should be dressed comfortably and for the weather.\nHikes cover 1-2 miles and last 1.5-2 hours.\nWell-behaved leashed pets are welcome to accompany their owners. In the rare case that a pet is disruptive or negatively impacts the experience\, the pet and its owner may be asked to excuse themselves from the guided walk.
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-10-17/
CATEGORIES:Guided Trail Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Birders-on-Cove-Hardwood-Trail-GSMNP-TN-Apr-16-1-1-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
